-- title:
--   Fuchsian translates of period data with Eichler level and generator
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N$, primes $q,q'$ with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$ and $q'\neq q$, and rationals $a,b$ such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order, i.e. a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning and finitely generated, maximal among such; let $N$ be squarefree and $R\le\Lambda$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ of maximal orders with relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$. Let $\iota$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map into $M_2(\mathbb{R})$, $L,M$ $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{C}^2$, $\tau$ in the upper half plane, and $c\neq0$ with $c\cdot L$ equal to the image $\Lambda_\tau$ of $\Lambda$ under the period map $x\mapsto \iota(x)\binom{\tau}{1}$ (entries complexified). Assume the level clause: for $\mathrm{lam}\in\Lambda$ and $r\in R$, if $N^{-1}\iota(\mathrm{lam})\binom{\tau}{1}\in c\cdot M$ then $N^{-1}\iota(\mathrm{lam}\,r)\binom{\tau}{1}\in c\cdot M$. Let $\gamma$ lie in `fuchsianGroup R ι`, the intersection of the image under $\iota$ of the subgroup of $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])^\times$ generated by the units satisfying `IsUnitOf R` with the kernel of the determinant. Let $m\in\mathbb{N}$, $v\in\mathbb{C}^2$ and $\xi_0\in\Lambda$ with $c\cdot v=m^{-1}\iota(\xi_0)\binom{\tau}{1}$. Then there are $c'\neq0$ and $u,w\in R$ with $uw=wu=1$, $\gamma=\iota(u)$ as matrices, $c'\cdot L=\Lambda_{\gamma\tau}$, the same level clause holding at $(\gamma\tau,c')$, and $c'\cdot v=m^{-1}\iota(\xi_0 w)\binom{\gamma\tau}{1}$.
--
--   This is the equivariance of quaternionic period data under the Fuchsian group attached to an Eichler order: the pair (period lattice, Eichler level structure) together with a full-level generator is carried by $\gamma=\iota(u)$ from $\tau$ to $\gamma\tau$, the generator's period coordinate being twisted on the right by $u^{-1}\in R$. It feeds the construction of algebraic families with extra level structure on Shimura curves in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
